      "id": "45460147",
      "title": "1_Joins - Introduction",
      "lectureOrder": 88,
      "videoOrder": 88,
      "sourceHash": "fd511cae15c31d923c262c67e61131e6fa342f6a127c5affe195be7f5a200d2d",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.22,
          "end": 2.03,
          "en": "Hi everyone!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.03,
          "end": 5.09,
          "en": "So far we completed the fundamentals of Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.12,
          "end": 8.66,
          "en": "Now we can focus on the advanced topics of Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.66,
          "end": 13.43,
          "en": "So we'll start off with Joinings Query builder Joinings to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.43,
          "end": 19.55,
          "en": "We already work with Query Builder, but we didn't work with the joints yet, so now we'll be working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.55,
          "end": 20.51,
          "en": "with joints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.54,
          "end": 21.98,
          "en": "Now what is joints?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.01,
          "end": 29.03,
          "en": "Joints are used to combine rows from two or more tables based on a related columns between them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.03,
          "end": 32.06,
          "en": "Thus mean with the joints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.06,
          "end": 40.01,
          "en": "You can establish connection between two or more tables, but there is condition you will be needing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.4,
          "end": 48.59,
          "en": "a reference column in both of the table and the values as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 48.98,
          "end": 49.76,
          "en": "Common values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 49.79,
          "end": 52.82,
          "en": "Both of the table should having a common value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 52.82,
          "end": 57.8,
          "en": "By that you will be able to establish a join between the tables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 58.22,
          "end": 61.79,
          "en": "We'll be talking about more about it later on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 62.18,
          "end": 65.27,
          "en": "Uh, for now, let's focus on this picture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 65.81,
          "end": 69.53,
          "en": "As you can see here, we have some joins, uh, join diagrams.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.53,
          "end": 72.53,
          "en": "You can say there are several type of join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 72.65,
          "end": 78.98,
          "en": "And if you already work with the MySQL, I hope you already familiar with, uh, query joins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78.98,
          "end": 85.28,
          "en": "So exactly the things that you can do with the MySQL joins, you will be able to do it in the query",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 85.28,
          "end": 86.66,
          "en": "builder joins as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 86.66,
          "end": 91.76,
          "en": "Just Query Builder give you a little bit more efficient way to, uh, do your work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 91.76,
          "end": 96.97999999999999,
          "en": "This means you have to write a little bit less amount of code when you are working with joins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 96.97999999999999,
          "end": 99.71000000000001,
          "en": "So as I said there are several types of joins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 99.71000000000001,
          "end": 103.72999999999999,
          "en": "So we'll be covering the mostly common joins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 103.88,
          "end": 107.3,
          "en": "So there are two type of join inner join and outer join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 107.3,
          "end": 113.78,
          "en": "In the outer join there are several parts as well like left join right join full join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 113.81,
          "end": 119.6,
          "en": "Obviously there are more joins, but if you cover these basic joins, you will get the idea for the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 119.63,
          "end": 124.13,
          "en": "rest of the joins as well So let's talk about the inner join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 124.18,
          "end": 126.16,
          "en": "Inner join means look at here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 126.16,
          "end": 129.01,
          "en": "Here we have two table table A table b.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 129.01,
          "end": 137.68,
          "en": "So if both of the table have a common value in them depending on this value we can establish a join",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 137.68,
          "end": 139.27,
          "en": "and it will be a inner join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 139.27,
          "end": 148.36,
          "en": "So in case of inner join it will give you only the rows that have matching values in both table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 148.39,
          "end": 149.29,
          "en": "That's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 149.65,
          "end": 154.21,
          "en": "You will get a more better uh idea when we will see some examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 154.21,
          "end": 156.94,
          "en": "But for now let's move on to the outer joins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 156.94,
          "end": 160.93,
          "en": "So in the outer joins we have the left join right join and full join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 160.96,
          "end": 163.42000000000002,
          "en": "Let's talk about left join first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 163.48,
          "end": 165.04,
          "en": "It's basically simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 165.04,
          "end": 167.23,
          "en": "We have again two table A b.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 167.32,
          "end": 169.09,
          "en": "Now if you want to access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 169.09,
          "end": 172.03,
          "en": "Or you can say create a join between A to B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 172.69,
          "end": 180.37,
          "en": "In that case it will be a left join because from the left table you are trying to join to the right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 180.4,
          "end": 181.12,
          "en": "table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 182.11,
          "end": 190.45,
          "en": "Okay let's say a table is a user table and b table is a order table, and if you want to get user's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 190.45,
          "end": 196.24,
          "en": "order, we can use a live join because I want user's order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 196.24,
          "end": 203.98,
          "en": "So from the user table I want a orders from another table from order tables actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 203.98,
          "end": 207.16,
          "en": "So we are accessing our data like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 207.46,
          "end": 209.59,
          "en": "So it is left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 209.59,
          "end": 211.66,
          "en": "So we call this joint left join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 211.66,
          "end": 213.46,
          "en": "Similar like left joint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 213.46,
          "end": 215.56,
          "en": "We have the right join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 215.56,
          "end": 222.31,
          "en": "So in this case if we uh try to access or you can say make join from right to left.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 222.31,
          "end": 227.26,
          "en": "That's been from let's say this one is a order table and this one is a user table from the order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 227.26,
          "end": 234.04,
          "en": "If you want to access the users, that which, uh, which users order, these are in that case it will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 234.07,
          "end": 235.99,
          "en": "we will be making a left join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 235.99,
          "end": 239.05,
          "en": "So it will be left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 240.13,
          "end": 240.76,
          "en": "Oh, sorry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 240.79,
          "end": 242.17,
          "en": "Right to left actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 242.17,
          "end": 245.32,
          "en": "So in that case we will be calling it right join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 245.32,
          "end": 246.94,
          "en": "And full join is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 246.94,
          "end": 247.27,
          "en": "That's mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 247.27,
          "end": 250.74,
          "en": "You will be making a full join of both of the tables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 252.15,
          "end": 254.85,
          "en": "You can see if you check the diagram.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 254.85,
          "end": 261.75,
          "en": "Actually, for the left join, we are accessing our data like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "Right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 263.22,
          "en": "Left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 263.22,
          "end": 266.94,
          "en": "For the right join we are doing right to left and in the full join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 266.94,
          "end": 272.01,
          "en": "We are doing the both left to right and right to left as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 272.01,
          "end": 273.63,
          "en": "So it is called full join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 273.63,
          "end": 279.09000000000003,
          "en": "So in the MySQL joins there isn't anything called full join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 279.12,
          "end": 287.01,
          "en": "Basically we use the combination of these two joins and we create a new join which is called full join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 287.1,
          "end": 289.53,
          "en": "So yeah that's pretty much it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 289.53,
          "end": 292.83,
          "en": "Uh, if you didn't understand, it's totally fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 292.83,
          "end": 299.85,
          "en": "Uh, when we you will see some examples, uh, you will get a better idea that what join does what.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 299.85,
          "end": 302.67,
          "en": "So we'll be obviously start off with the inner join.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 302.67,
          "end": 306.9,
          "en": "Then one by one we'll be covering each of the joins in our upcoming lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 306.9,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "So that's it for this video and I will see you in the next one.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
